import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import Figure from '../components/Figure.astro';
import Calc from '../components/Calc.astro';
const faq = [
 {
  "q": "What is the 8th Pay Commission salary at Level 10?",
  "a": "It has not been announced. Level 10 entry basic pay is Rs 56,100 today. Illustrative scenarios give Rs 1,07,700 at 1.92, Rs 1,27,900 at 2.28, Rs 1,44,200 at 2.57 and Rs 1,60,400 at 2.86. These are multiples, not government figures."
 },
 {
  "q": "What is the in-hand salary at Level 10 today?",
  "a": "At the entry cell in a Class X city, gross pay is about Rs 1,14,141 and in-hand pay is about Rs 1,04,997 after a 10% NPS or UPS contribution, before CGHS, CGEGIS and tax. Your payslip is the final authority."
 },
 {
  "q": "Will DA be added to my Level 10 basic pay?",
  "a": "That has not been decided. Past commissions absorbed DA through the fitment factor. If that happens again, a factor of 1.63 would only match today's basic plus DA of Rs 91,443, so the real gain at Level 10 is the factor minus 1.63 as a share of 1.63."
 }
];
const toc = [{"id": "today", "label": "Level 10 pay today (7th CPC)"}, {"id": "scenarios", "label": "Level 10 salary under 8th CPC scenarios"}, {"id": "progression", "label": "Level 10 pay matrix: first 10 cells"}, {"id": "promotion", "label": "What promotion or MACP is worth at Level 10"}, {"id": "estimate", "label": "Estimate your own Level 10 salary under the 8th CPC"}, {"id": "faq", "label": "FAQ"}];
const related = ["8th-pay-commission-salary-calculator", "8th-pay-commission-pay-matrix", "fitment-factor-8th-pay-commission", "8th-pay-commission-level-9-salary", "8th-pay-commission-level-11-salary"];
---

<SiteLayout title="8th Pay Commission Level 10 Salary: Pay Matrix and Estimates" description="Level 10 basic pay is Rs 56,100 today. See 8th Pay Commission Level 10 salary at 1.92, 2.28, 2.57 and 2.86 fitment, with cells, DA, HRA and promotion pay." slug="8th-pay-commission-level-10-salary" h1="8th Pay Commission Level 10 Salary" lead="Level 10 pay today, the first 10 matrix cells, scenario pay and what promotion is worth." faq={faq} toc={toc} related={related} pageType="article" breadcrumbLabel="Level 10 Salary">

<div class="answer"><p><strong>Short answer:</strong> Level 10 entry basic pay is Rs 56,100 a month under the 7th CPC, or Rs 91,443 with DA at 63%. The 8th CPC has not announced a fitment factor. At illustrative factors of 1.92 to 2.86, entry basic would be Rs 1,07,700 to Rs 1,60,400.</p></div>

<h2 id="today">Level 10 pay today (7th CPC)</h2>
<p>Level 10 is used for entry-level Group A officers, including those recruited to the all-India and central services. The entry cell is Rs 56,100 a month. The table below adds DA at 63% (from 1 July 2026), HRA at the current 30 / 20 / 10 rates and Transport Allowance with DA (base slab for a city that is not in the higher-TPTA list).</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Component</th><th class="num">Class X city</th><th class="num">Class Y city</th><th class="num">Class Z city</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Basic pay (entry cell)</th><td class="num">₹56,100</td><td class="num">₹56,100</td><td class="num">₹56,100</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Dearness Allowance (63%)</th><td class="num">₹35,343</td><td class="num">₹35,343</td><td class="num">₹35,343</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">HRA (30% / 20% / 10%)</th><td class="num">₹16,830</td><td class="num">₹11,220</td><td class="num">₹5,610</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Transport Allowance with DA</th><td class="num">₹5,868</td><td class="num">₹5,868</td><td class="num">₹5,868</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><strong>Gross monthly pay</strong></th><td class="num">₹1,14,141</td><td class="num">₹1,08,531</td><td class="num">₹1,02,921</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>With NPS or UPS contribution of 10% of basic plus DA (Rs 9,144), a Class X employee at the entry cell would take home about <strong>Rs 1,04,997</strong> before CGHS, CGEGIS and any tax. Use the calculator below with your own cell and city.</p><Calc name="cgsalary" title="Level 10 salary calculator" intro="Move the cell to see how annual increments change gross pay. Rates are the current 7th CPC rates." preset={{"level": "10"}} />

<h2 id="scenarios">Level 10 salary under 8th CPC scenarios</h2>
<Figure name="level-10-salary-scenarios" /><p>The 8th Pay Commission has not announced a fitment factor, a pay matrix or a payment date. The table applies the four scenarios used across this site, plus the staff-side demand, to the entry cell and to cell 10, and rounds to the nearest Rs 100 as a matrix would.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Fitment factor</th><th class="num">Entry-cell basic</th><th class="num">Rise over today's basic</th><th class="num">Gain over basic + DA today</th><th class="num">Basic at cell 10 (after 9 increments)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">1.92</th><td class="num">₹1,07,700</td><td class="num">+92%</td><td class="num">+17.8%</td><td class="num">₹1,40,500</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">2.28</th><td class="num">₹1,27,900</td><td class="num">+128%</td><td class="num">+39.9%</td><td class="num">₹1,66,900</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">2.57</th><td class="num">₹1,44,200</td><td class="num">+157%</td><td class="num">+57.7%</td><td class="num">₹1,88,100</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">2.86</th><td class="num">₹1,60,400</td><td class="num">+186%</td><td class="num">+75.4%</td><td class="num">₹2,09,400</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">3.83 (staff demand)</th><td class="num">₹2,14,900</td><td class="num">+283%</td><td class="num">+135.0%</td><td class="num">₹2,80,400</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The last-but-one column is the one that matters. Today the same employee draws Rs 91,443 (basic plus 63% DA). A factor of 1.63 would only restore that total; the real gain is the part above it. At 2.28 the gain at Level 10 is about 40%, and at 1.92 about 18%. See <a href="/da-merger-8th-pay-commission/">DA merger</a> for why.</p>

<h2 id="progression">Level 10 pay matrix: first 10 cells</h2>
<p>Level 10 is where officers enter Group A. Probationers start at the first cell and move up through annual increments while they train and settle into their service.</p><p>The next level (Level 11, the senior time scale) is reached after a few years of service, so the progression table is useful for planning how pay will build up through the early career.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Cell</th><th class="num">Basic pay</th><th class="num">Increase over the cell before</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">1</th><td class="num">₹56,100</td><td class="num">-</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">2</th><td class="num">₹57,800</td><td class="num">+₹1,700</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">3</th><td class="num">₹59,500</td><td class="num">+₹1,700</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">4</th><td class="num">₹61,300</td><td class="num">+₹1,800</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">5</th><td class="num">₹63,100</td><td class="num">+₹1,800</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">6</th><td class="num">₹65,000</td><td class="num">+₹1,900</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">7</th><td class="num">₹67,000</td><td class="num">+₹2,000</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">8</th><td class="num">₹69,000</td><td class="num">+₹2,000</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">9</th><td class="num">₹71,100</td><td class="num">+₹2,100</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">10</th><td class="num">₹73,200</td><td class="num">+₹2,100</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Each cell is the one before it plus 3%, rounded to the nearest Rs 100, and the increment falls once a year. The full list of levels is in the <a href="/8th-pay-commission-pay-matrix/">pay matrix guide</a>, and you can look up any cell with the lookup tool there.</p>

<h2 id="promotion">What promotion or MACP is worth at Level 10</h2>
<p>On promotion, pay is fixed in the next level at the first cell that is at least one increment above the current pay. The same method is used when the <a href="/macp-scheme-explained/">MACP scheme</a> gives a financial upgrade after 10, 20 or 30 years without promotion.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th class="num">Pay now</th><th class="num">After one increment</th><th class="num">Fixed in Level 11 at</th><th class="num">Monthly gain in basic</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Promotion at cell 1</th><td class="num">₹56,100</td><td class="num">₹57,800</td><td class="num">₹67,700 (cell 1)</td><td class="num">₹11,600</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Promotion or MACP at cell 10 (about 9 years in the level)</th><td class="num">₹73,200</td><td class="num">₹75,400</td><td class="num">₹76,200 (cell 5)</td><td class="num">₹3,000</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Level 9 entry pay: ₹53,100, which is ₹3,000 lower than Level 10.</li><li>Level 11 entry pay: ₹67,700, which is ₹11,600 higher than Level 10.</li></ul><p>Figures use the 7th CPC pay matrix as rebuilt from the 3% rule and are for illustration. Your department's promotion rules and the official matrix decide your actual pay.</p>

<h2 id="estimate">Estimate your own Level 10 salary under the 8th CPC</h2>
<Calc name="salary" title="8th Pay Commission salary at Level 10" intro="Choose a fitment scenario and city class. The level and entry basic are already set for Level 10." preset={{"level": "10", "basic": 56100}} /><p>See the same breakdown for other levels: <a href="/8th-pay-commission-level-1-salary/">Level 1</a>, <a href="/8th-pay-commission-level-3-salary/">Level 3</a>, <a href="/8th-pay-commission-level-5-salary/">Level 5</a>, <a href="/8th-pay-commission-level-6-salary/">Level 6</a>, <a href="/8th-pay-commission-level-7-salary/">Level 7</a>, <a href="/8th-pay-commission-level-8-salary/">Level 8</a>, <a href="/8th-pay-commission-level-9-salary/">Level 9</a>, <a href="/8th-pay-commission-level-11-salary/">Level 11</a>.</p>

</SiteLayout>
